  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book is a limited-edition hand-bound artist book. Original photographs, poetry and text by Laura Russell. Digital printing with archival inks on archival paper. Flyleaves are stained by Tyvek. Interior pages burned by hand. Plywood covers hinged with book cloth. Hand bound at Laura's studio, Simply Books, Ltd."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Title from verso of title page:  Urban decay a photographic essay.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Savannah College of Art and Design own edition number 16/25. Signed by the author/book artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Material Specifications: Archival digital printing on Janus Duo Card paper, stained Tyvek flyleaves, plywood covers. Enclosed in a chip-board wrapper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Typography: ITC Franklin Gothic.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In Laura Russell's hometown of Saginaw, Michigan, decades of poverty and the decline of the automobile business are creating tan urban blight that is heartbreaking. Lost factory jobs lead to lost homes as families struggle to survive....Urban decay presents 30 photographs, all taken on one cold morning, in one small neighborhood - an area about 7 blocks by 3 blocks. Two poems, introductory text and a map of the burned out houses accompany the photographs..."--Accompanying Information Sheet.</subfield>
